Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:34:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(sdk): report the account's code in
 getAuthorityStatus (EIP-7702, EIP-7851)

getAuthorityStatus now also reads the account's code through the Ethereum
module's optional getCode and reports its kind: none, an EIP-7702 delegation
indicator (0xef0100 || delegate), an EIP-7851 ECDSA-disabled indicator
(0xef0101 || delegate) or other code, with the delegate. The classification is
Profile H2's: only an exact 23-byte indicator counts. accountCode is undefined
when the module cannot read code. Wallets can show an ECDSA-disabled account
next to its retirement and E1 successor state.

Decryption Authority Lifecycle, Phase 4 P1.6.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
